{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 1, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.2-3b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a prince of the House of Lusignan and the ruler of the County of Tripoli from 1152 until his death in 1187. He was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and his wife Adelaide of Ibelin. Raymond III was born around 1145 in Beirut Lebanon. \n\n* **Early Life and Reign ** \nRaymond III became the Count of Tripoli at the age of seven after his father's death in 1152. He was raised by his mother and a regency council until he came of age. In 1160 Raymond III married Eschiva II of Jerusalem a niece of King Amalric I of Jerusalem. Raymond III's reign was marked by conflict with the neighboring city-state of Aleppo. In 1168 Raymond III allied himself with the Byzantine Empire to fight against Aleppo. \n\n* **Military Campaigns ** \nDuring his reign Raymond III led several military campaigns against the Ayyubid dynasty. In 1168 Raymond III allied himself with the Byzantine Empire in a war against Aleppo. Raymond III's forces suffered a defeat in 1172. In 1174 Raymond III allied himself with the Ayyubid dynasty's enemy the Zengid dynasty. However the alliance was short lived and Raymond III's forces were defeated by the Ayyubids. \n\n* **Death and Legacy ** \nRaymond III was killed in the Battle of Hattin on July 4 1187. He was struck by a crossbow bolt while fleeing from the battle. Raymond III's death was a significant blow to the County of Tripoli. Raymond III was succeeded by his 16 year old son Bohemond IV.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.0016098171472549438}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -0.0001308832288486883}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.16895784437656403}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -3.802703940891661e-05}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -0.0002967870968859643}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -7.068861305015162e-05}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.0